---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Membership preview · Strewnfields"
  description="A transparent preview of possible future Strewnfields research membership, with no signup, payment, or private data in this release."
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Concept preview · No signup or payment</p>
      <h1>Research tools, when the evidence can scale.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The public catalogue comes first. A future membership may support a larger reviewed
        catalogue, advanced spatial search, exports, and research workflows.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="membership-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Possible future workspace</p>
        <h2>Built around provenance, not hidden map pins.</h2>
        <p>
          Any member product will keep free examples on stable public URLs and preserve the
          same source, confidence, precision, and safety rules.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Under consideration</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Search across a much larger editorially reviewed catalogue</li>
          <li>Claim comparison and saved research views</li>
          <li>Source-aware spatial filters and documented exports</li>
          <li>Revision alerts and correction workflows</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What is deliberately absent</h2>
      <p>
        There is no account creation, checkout, price, testimonial, or waiting-list data
        collection in this release. Those details require product, legal, privacy,
        operational, and support decisions that have not been made.
      </p>
      <h2>Private means server-side</h2>
      <p>
        Future restricted data must live behind server-side authorization. It will not be
        shipped in static JSON, JavaScript, GeoJSON, source maps, or public Git history.
        Protected locations remain protected regardless of subscription status.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
